 iron, to prevent deficiencies and is instrumental in modifying the composition of the microbiota, which can affect obesity. For patients with cystic fibrosis, dietary adjustments are necessary to ensure adequate energy and nutrient absorption. Similarly, older adults may require specific dietary regimens to manage weight and overall health effectively.\n\nThe dietary practices associated with \"DIETA\" also extend to managing chronic conditions, such as diabetes, where individuals must adhere to specific nutritional plans to maintain health and regulate blood sugar levels. For patients with glucose-galactose malabsorption, strict dietary adherence is essential to avoid symptoms, while those with fructan intolerance must engage in careful dietary management involving the elimination and gradual reintroduction of fructans.\n\nIn the context of cardiovascular health, \"DIETA\" refers to dietary patterns that can influence health outcomes, including cholesterol levels. It also addresses the dietary components that affect the absorption and metabolism of medications, highlighting the importance of food selection in relation to nutrition, especially in enteral feeding contexts.\n\nFurthermore, \"DIETA\" includes dietary recommendations for individuals with specific conditions such as galactosemia, where a galactose-free diet is crucial to prevent complications, and phenylketonuria, which requires lifelong restrictions on foods high in phenylalanine. The guidelines also consider the dietary needs of children, focusing on nutrition and health, and emphasize the importance of managing dietary factors that may contribute to the development of conditions like Type 1 Diabetes.\n\nOverall, \"DIETA\" represents a multifaceted approach to nutrition, emphasizing the significance of tailored dietary practices in managing health outcomes across a spectrum of medical conditions.", "CÓDIGO DE MENÚS:A practical application of dietary codes through menus that detail the foods included in various diets.", "PLATOS:Dishes that are part of the dietary menus, which must meet nutritional and safety standards.", "COSTUMBRES GASTRONÓMICAS:COSTUMBRES GASTRONÓMICAS refers to the culinary customs and traditions of a region that play a significant role in shaping dietary preferences and acceptance among individuals, particularly in the context of hospitalized patients. When planning diets for these patients, it is essential to consider these culinary customs to ensure that the meals are not only nutritionally adequate but also culturally appropriate, thereby promoting acceptance and compliance with dietary recommendations.", "FICHAS TÉCNICAS:FICHAS TÉCNICAS refers to technical sheets that provide detailed information about the composition, preparation, and nutritional value of dishes served in the hospital. These sheets serve as a comprehensive resource for understanding the ingredients and nutritional content of the meals offered, ensuring that dietary needs and health standards are met.", "DIETA BASAL:The Basal Diet, known as \"DIETA BASAL,\" is the most requested diet in hospitals, specifically designed to meet the general nutritional needs of patients. It serves as the basic hospital menu and is intended for patients who do not require any special modifications to their diet. This diet ensures that patients receive essential nutrients while maintaining a standard dietary framework suitable for a wide range of individuals in a hospital setting.", "DIETAS TERAPÉUTICAS:\"DIETAS TERAPÉUTICAS\" refers to specialized diets that are specifically designed to meet the energy and nutrient requirements of hospitalized patients. These therapeutic diets are derived from a basal diet and are tailored to address the unique nutritional needs of individual patients, ensuring that they receive the appropriate nutrients necessary for their recovery and overall health.", "DIETA DE TEXTURA MODIFICADA TRADICIONAL:A traditional modified texture diet that uses natural foods, altering their texture and consistency for patients with swallowing difficulties.", "DIETA DE TEXTURA MODIFICADA COMERCIAL:A commercial modified texture diet used when traditional adaptations are insufficient to meet nutritional needs.", "HORARIOS DE PETICIÓN:Schedules for requesting, distributing, and collecting meals in a hospital setting.", "ALIMENTACIÓN ADAPTADA:Adapted nutrition strategies for patients with specific dietary needs, particularly those with swallowing difficulties."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}